- a) A clear and concise description of the product or goods, including its features, price, specifications, warnings and dimensions which may include GTIN;
- b) The final consumer price should be displayed in an easy and accessible format at the checkout page and shall include the breakdown of the price with all its components including any applicable taxes, shipping fees, and other charges;
- c) Privacy policy, and terms and conditions of use, in compliance with applicable law;
- d) Cancellation, exchange, return, or refund, compensation policies that specify the charges therein and the time limit of all products or services (together, ‘Goods’) on the platform;
- e) Information on the presence of a reporting and returning mechanism for counterfeit products which may require extended timelines beyond the generic return timelines stated above;
- f) Any applicable restrictions, limitations or conditions of purchase, including geographic limitations, resale prohibitions, or parental/guardian approval or supervision requirements for minors;
- g) Any applicable restrictions, limitations or conditions usage, warnings for hazardous content for users;
- h) Clear indication from the seller regarding manufacturer/importer, seller and country of origin or origins (in case the country of origin would differ for goods of different batches);
- j) Terms and Conditions of discounts or special offers, and the details to avail of same;
- k) Details of payment options available to the consumer to complete the transaction;



- m) Seller information including but not limited
to contact details, trade names, principal address of headquarters, nodal grievance redressal officers, customer care toll-free number, customer care email address;

- n) Policy for wrong delivery and non-delivery and terms of sale stating clearly whether the product is returnable or not;
- p) Customer reviews and ratings, which are an essential source of information for other potential customers, and e-commerce platforms should display them;
- q) The ability to compare products based on features, prices, and other criteria can help customers make informed purchasing decisions, if applicable;
- r) Disclosure of the materials used in the product, wherever applicable, including whether they are natural, synthetic, or a blend of both;
- s) Buyer protection policy which details the process for registering and resolving complaint(s) raised by the consumer for unsatisfactory experience;
- t) Other relevant information, such as the brand and model of the product, materials used, care instructions, and any relevant certifications or standards, applicable product licenses, should be provided at a prominent place near the listing; and
- u) Provide a search function that allows customers to search for products by name, category, country of origin or keyword to help them quickly find what they are looking for.
